# DEPRECATED — state.yaml is retired.
#
# Per-chat WhatsApp config now lives in ~/.hermes/config.yaml as the SINGLE
# source of truth (DRY). This file is kept only as a schema reference. The
# plugin no longer reads or writes state.yaml.
#
# WHERE THINGS LIVE NOW
# ---------------------
# 1) Operator identity  ->  top-level `whatsapp_admins` in config.yaml:
#
#      whatsapp_admins:
#        root: YOUR_NUMBER@s.whatsapp.net   # permanent admin, never removable
#        extra: []                          # managed by /admin add|remove
#
# 2) Per-chat behaviour  ->  fields ON each chat's route under
#    `gateway.profile_routes` in config.yaml:
#
#      gateway:
#        profile_routes:
#          - name: cgpt-5
#            platform: whatsapp
#            chat_id: 120363406938117817@g.us
#            profile: cgpt
#            reply: true          # was reply_whitelist  (/whitelist add|remove)
#            no_mention: false    # was no_mention_groups (/no-mention add|remove)
#            paused: false        # was paused_chats MANUAL pause (pause/resume)
#            pause_reason: ""      # optional label when paused: true
#
#    Field semantics (unchanged behaviour):
#      - reply: true       -> bot replies here (else silent-save only).
#      - no_mention: true  -> group replies WITHOUT an @mention (needs reply:true
#                             + a group + core whatsapp.require_mention: false).
#      - paused: true      -> MANUAL pause. Automated handoff-pause is separate
#                             and still derived live from concierge.db.
#      - profile           -> which bot serves the chat. Now HOT: the listener
#                             stamps source.profile from a live config.yaml
#                             re-read, so moving a chat's profile needs NO restart.
#
# admin_groups is DROPPED — admins are resolved by identity and can run ops
# commands anywhere.
#
# All of the above is managed at runtime by in-chat commands (and by cupbots-hub),
# which write config.yaml atomically via config_routes.py (ruamel, comment-safe).
